nodes:
- _type: Monitor
  name: Model end-to-end latency
  identifier: urn:stackpack:suse-ai:monitor:vllm-high-e2e-latency
  description: P99 latency for each vLLM model deployment, aggregated across its runtime replicas.
  intervalSeconds: 60
  status: ENABLED
  function: urn:stackpack:common:monitor-function:topological-threshold
  arguments:
    threshold: 30.0
    comparator: GT
    failureState: DEVIATING
    queries:
      topologyQuery: type = "genai served model" and label = "stackpack:suse-ai" and label = "suse.ai.product:vllm"
      promqlQuery: histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le)
        (rate({__name__=~"vllm(:|_)e2e_request_latency_seconds_bucket",
        service_namespace="${tags.service.namespace}", service_name="${tags.service.name}",
        model_name="${tags.vllm.model.name}"}[5m])))
      aliasTemplate: Model end-to-end latency
      unit: s
    titleTemplate: Model end-to-end latency
  remediationHint: Inspect model latency and throughput, then open the inference service to check its queue and GPU
    cache. Compare traces for slow requests. Tune the model, token limits or serving capacity for the application
    latency budget.
